vides software platforms to run in hybrid, public or private clouds, and multi-cloud environments in the United States and internationally. It primarily offers Elasticsearch Platform, a set of software products that ingest and store data from various sources and formats, as well as performs search, analysis, and visualization on that data. The company also provides Elastic search product a distributed, real-time vector database and analytics engine and data store for all types of data, including textual, numerical, geospatial, structured, and unstructured; Kibana, a user interface, management, and configuration interface for the platforms; Search & AI, a platform with retrieval algorithms and the ability to integrate with large language models; and elastic security, a security solution that provides unified protection to prevent, detect, and respond to threats. In addition, it offers Elastic Observability, a solution that brings unified datastore, including Logs analytics to search, analyze, and visualize petabytes of structured and unstructured logs; infrastructure monitoring to gain visibility across cloud, on-premises, Kubernetes, serverless, and hosts; Application Performance Monitoring to support native production-grade; digital experience monitoring; large language models; and Elastic Cloud, a cloud-based subscription offering such as Elastic Cloud Hosted and Elastic Cloud Serverless. The company was incorporated in 2012 and is based in Amsterdam, the Netherlands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ashutosh  Kulkarni | CEO & Executive Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $447K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 30%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $77K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Elastic N.V. is a mid-cap technology business with a $8.9B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +5.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -13% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 73% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $322M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.89\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 8.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 252% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.52278776025788},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $420.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Elastic (NYSE:ESTC) Use AI Demand To Widen Its Reach?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/artificial-intelligence/can-elastic-nyseestc-use-ai-demand-to-widen-its-reach","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795531500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"All You Need to Know About Elastic (ESTC) Rating Upgrade to Buy","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034019/all-you-need-to-know-about-elastic-estc-rating-upgrade-to-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3034019","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795449604.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Precision Trading with Elastic N.v. (ESTC) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Precision_Trading_with_Elastic_N.v._ESTC_Risk_Zones_112126124001_1795239601.html","date